{"id": "en_lost_forest_p1", "total": 64.61, "segments": [{"text": "If you are lost in a dark forest at dusk, never hike toward a distant wooden cabin.", "start": 0.0, "end": 3.82}, {"text": "Cole is lost, and thick snow starts falling fast across the frozen woods around him now.", "start": 4.4, "end": 7.94}, {"text": "Night is coming in 20 minutes, but walking further will only make his danger much worse.", "start": 8.5, "end": 11.96}, {"text": "Searchers always start looking from your last known point, so Cole stays put near trees.", "start": 12.6, "end": 16.3}, {"text": "One. Cole stops moving immediately to follow the proven S.T.O.P. rule: Stop, Think, Observe, Plan.", "start": 16.92, "end": 22.26}, {"text": "He checks his cold surroundings and chooses a safe spot right next to a thick tree.", "start": 22.8, "end": 26.1}, {"text": "Two. Cole makes himself visible and audible in the open while staying near shelter.", "start": 26.74, "end": 30.18}, {"text": "He pulls out his bright orange jacket and crouches to remain clearly visible.", "start": 30.7, "end": 33.6}, {"text": "He blows 3 sharp whistle blasts into the cold air, the official signal for distress.", "start": 33.98, "end": 37.54}, {"text": "Three. Before total darkness arrives, Cole gets off the freezing cold ground without delay.", "start": 38.3, "end": 42.22}, {"text": "He gathers pine branches and dry leaves to build an insulating pad under his body.", "start": 42.7, "end": 45.96}, {"text": "He crouches tight against the wide tree trunk to shield himself from bitter wind.", "start": 46.44, "end": 49.38}, {"text": "Cole stays visible and waits quietly for the search and rescue team to locate him.", "start": 50.1, "end": 53.2}, {"text": "It was the perfect survival plan, but there was just one very serious problem.", "start": 53.2, "end": 57.36}, {"text": "The heavy snow is rapidly covering his bright jacket and hiding him from searchers.", "start": 57.86, "end": 61.46}], "words": [["If", 0.0, 0.26], ["y